<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">La Alcudia (Elche)</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ilici</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">La Alcudia is an archaeological site 2 km south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elche">Elche</a> in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, the remains of the Iberian town of Ilici and the Roman colony of Colonia Iulia Ilici Augusta. Settled from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze-age">Bronze Age</a> to the Visigothic period, it was a centre of the Contestani. The stone bust known as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lady-of-elche">Lady of Elche</a> was found there in 1897.</p></div>
